+// GDN decode conv: the depthwise causal conv window (state ++ x) is read
+// from two buffers in one kernel and the shifted carry-out state is
+// written in-kernel, replacing the two Concatenate copies plus the
+// contiguous state view the composed path materializes. Decode (T == 1)
+// only; larger T falls back to the composed concatenate + conv1d.
+// `activate` applies silu to the conv output (the model's nn.silu) inside
+// the same dispatch: the fused kernel rounds the conv output, the
+// sigmoid, and the product exactly like the composed chain, and the
+// fallback composes out * sigmoid(out).
+// `qk_key_dim > 0` additionally folds the GDN q/k per-head rms_norm_scaled
+// calls into the same dispatch (the model's q = rms_norm_scaled(q, None,
+// inv_scale^2, eps); k = rms_norm_scaled(k, None, inv_scale, eps) over
+// 128-channel head-rows of the first 2*qk_key_dim channels). The fused
+// kernel reproduces the FastNormGatedBF16 mode-1 reduction and rounding
+// exactly; the fallback composes the exact model ops. The wrapper refuses
+// qk work it cannot fuse (loudly, per the omarchy error contract): the
+// kernel needs count % 256 == 0 and qk_key_dim % 256 == 0, and the caller
+// guarantees head_dim == 128.
